# CLI reference

The workspace provides `rocci` for templates, documents, runtime apps, and
bundles, plus `rocs` for static documentation sites.

Examples below use `cargo run` from a source checkout. Installed binaries use
the same arguments without the Cargo prefix.

## Validate configuration

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- validate [rocci.toml]
```

Parse and validate the application configuration. Unknown fields and unsafe
runtime settings are errors.

## Build source to Roc

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- build INPUT [-o OUTPUT]
```

Accepts `.rocci` or `.rocdown`. Without `-o`, generated Roc is printed to
standard output. Theme and color-scheme flags apply to Rocdown's default shell.

## Inspect source

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- inspect [--ast] INPUT
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- ast INPUT
```

`inspect` reports components, fixtures, page and route metadata, source-map
segments, and generated Roc. `--ast` adds the parse tree. `ast` prints only the
LISPy parse tree.

## Run an app

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- run [OPTIONS] [FILE_OR_DIRECTORY] [-- ROC_ARGS...]
```

The input may be a standalone `.rocci` or `.rocdown` file, a directory, or an
authored `main.roc`. The default input is `main.roc`.

| Option | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `--no-window` | Serve without opening the embedded window |
| `--port PORT` | Override the listening port |
| `--theme THEME` | Select a default Rocdown CSS theme |
| `--color-scheme auto|light|dark` | Set Rocdown color policy |

`ROC_BASIC_WEBSERVER_PORT` can also override the server port.

## Preview one component

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- view FILE \
  --component NAME \
  --arg name=value
```

Arguments may repeat. Component names accept authored PascalCase or lowered
camelCase.

## Browse components

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- browse [ROOTS...]
```

Discover `.rocci` files recursively and open the component and fixture browser.

## Manage Datastar

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- datastar pin VERSION --app PATH
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- datastar update --app PATH
```

Pin copies an exact supported version into the application's configured assets.
Update resolves the latest release explicitly. Normal `run` never auto-upgrades.

## Bundle a desktop app

```sh
cargo run -p rocci-cli -- bundle --config rocci.toml
```

Build a local ad-hoc-signed macOS app bundle. Other packaging targets are not
implemented yet.

## Build documentation

```sh
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- build [ROOT] [--output DIRECTORY]
```

The default root is the current directory. `ROOT` may be a documentation
directory or a `.rocdown` file. A file root uses the parent directory as the
content root and still discovers sibling pages and assets. `rocs.toml` is
optional. `--output` overrides `build.output`.

```sh
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- build report.rocdown --output dist
```

Local `@img` and Markdown image paths resolve against the source file. Missing
local files fail the catalog (`RD2103`). Files under `build.assets` are
content-hashed whether the authored URL is `/assets/foo.png` or
`assets/foo.png`.

## Preview documentation

```sh
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- run [ROOT] [--port PORT] [--no-window] [--output DIRECTORY]
```

Watch `.rocdown` sources, `rocs.toml`, and assets, rebuild, and serve the site
with live reload. The default root is the current directory. A `.rocdown` file
root uses the same parent-directory rule as `build`. Preview output
goes to a temp directory unless `--output` is set, so a production `dist/` is
not overwritten.

```sh
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- run report.rocdown
```

| Option | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `--no-window` | Serve without opening the embedded window |
| `--port PORT` | Override the listening port |
| `--output DIRECTORY` | Write preview files here instead of a temp directory |

Port defaults to a free port with the embedded window, or `8000` with
`--no-window`. `ROC_BASIC_WEBSERVER_PORT` can also override the server port.

Content edits rebuild the static HTML. The Rocci theme is recompiled only when
generated Roc changes (titles, headings, navigation, theme CSS, docs component
titles). Included snippet files also trigger a rebuild. Dynamic islands are
not live-reloaded; pages that use them still fail the catalog.

## Check documentation

```sh
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- check [ROOT] [--format terminal|json]
```

Validate the catalog, including `@docs` content models, includes, page links,
and local assets, without compiling Roc or writing output. `ROOT` may be a
directory or a `.rocdown` file.

## Test documented examples

```sh
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- test [ROOT] [--update] [--format terminal|json]
```

Run `@docs example` commands that declare `test`. This is not part of
`rocs build`. `--update` rewrites golden files named by `expect`.

## Validate and build knowledge

```sh
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- knowledge check [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci] [--format terminal|json]
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- knowledge inspect catalog [ROOT]
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- knowledge inspect concept ID [ROOT]
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- knowledge inspect graph [ROOT]
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- knowledge search QUERY [ROOT]
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- knowledge build [ROOT] [--output DIRECTORY]
cargo run -p rocs-cli -- knowledge run [ROOT] [--profile base|rocci] [--port PORT] [--no-window] [--output DIRECTORY]
```

`knowledge inspect catalog` and `knowledge search` accept repeatable `--type`,
`--tag`, `--status`, `--authority`, and `--trust-tier` filters plus
`--stale true|false`. Alternatives within type, status, authority, and trust
tier are ORed; repeated tags are all required. Search matches all query words
against metadata and heading chunks. Derived trust tiers are
`human-reviewed`, `generated`, and `unverified`.

The default root is `knowledge`. Base mode checks OKF v0.2 without imposing
Rocci's repository vocabulary. Rocci mode additionally requires the approved
types, tags, lifecycle, provenance, authority, and owner fields. The build
validates before writing static HTML, `catalog.json`, `search.json`,
`llms.txt`, and `validation.json`; knowledge Markdown is never executed as Roc
or Rocci.
`knowledge run` watches Markdown records, rebuilds the bundle, serves its
generated site with the standard Rocs theme, and live-reloads after successful
changes. Bundle links are mapped to clean routes and linked non-Markdown files
are served alongside the pages. Preview output uses a temporary directory
unless `--output` is set.
